            <ArticleTitle>Monitoring post-operative effects in day-surgery patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study was undertaken in the day surgical unit to ascertain the morbidity following herniorrhaphy in adult patients. The results showed a reduction in recovery time of 50 minutes when bupivacaine hydrochloride was used. Interestingly, patients given diclofenac sodium and bupivacaine hydrochloride showed no difference in the pain experienced post-operatively from those given only bupivacaine hydrochloride.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
